lane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,5,-1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,2.5,1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128464/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128464"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection/c54dad43ccfa48b4a3536a4cd3148c1de53ef1cb872f5d1e6d3b3a672532bbd1" :answer/id #uuid "b27c84a1-e656-5cb8-95cc-b98182a489fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection/dd7305ad1689fa12dfc52790fcff04025b45beb791f6d68ebcfe242595ca5aaf" :answer/id #uuid "9218ba11-a571-5866-a396-17af641139b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection/1a9dde270eea3efcfcb72731155508a6b48ef726ce4bc5d7c49159affcbfdee6" :answer/id #uuid "5a2686ea-6935-5f28-b5a3-bfca91494284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection/42c8de8f35a2973b0df6f8fb56062167a97d78d235d94c600de25f3b81969af0" :answer/id #uuid "22f93ffe-e35d-55ff-ab2b-3ecd64706980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=s[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "8181d921-1a85-542a-822e-36d04f627f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f94e8405-4a0e-5325-b14d-662978404d2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70968/selection/1a9dde270eea3efcfcb72731155508a6b48ef726ce4bc5d7c49159affcbfdee6" :answer-field/choices ["q-70968/selection/c54dad43ccfa48b4a3536a4cd3148c1de53ef1cb872f5d1e6d3b3a672532bbd1" "q-70968/selection/dd7305ad1689fa12dfc52790fcff04025b45beb791f6d68ebcfe242595ca5aaf" "q-70968/selection/1a9dde270eea3efcfcb72731155508a6b48ef726ce4bc5d7c49159affcbfdee6" "q-70968/selection/42c8de8f35a2973b0df6f8fb56062167a97d78d235d94c600de25f3b81969af0" "q-70968/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70968" :question/id #uuid "77d373ff-47a1-54e3-92e9-7a36969b64d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70968" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $S(3,-1,0)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $S$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70968/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33818"] :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,0,-1⟩+t⟨-2,-7,5⟩+s⟨2,12,5⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,-7,5⟩$ and $w=⟨2,12,5⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-95i+20j-10k \\\\  & =⟨-95,20,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-95,20,-10⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128495/selection/c6dd2d15eb4b719eec5fadf89c49c6c2439a70f23f5c6605af2144fd37987376" :answer/id #uuid "0c037ba7-7eb0-5242-84b2-3bf2f2cc670e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128495/selection/22e2aa3be7cb2d07c61177a8b1331446ab72d7ef30045cc92794ef01586ed3ae" :answer/id #uuid "c394f154-7da4-5fd6-8df5-0f0b623511a3" :a