do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-9i-j-23k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128495/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33158"] :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-2,23,14)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-3,5,1⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $r=⟨-30,55,25⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨4,7,-1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-2,23,14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-2,23,14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection/f713e3c51be20750b1705399d88e20c65c6db6c19140d6bc7085e3e11b48f828" :answer/id #uuid "dff53a4c-b48b-5747-b163-31962cf36196" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection/2bf6099f6a9973b8307e08f883a440474edbb996ec474204a39fc02ae75563ab" :answer/id #uuid "d37fbf35-1ec1-53b4-908a-7745d3148217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection/4d0ae1d7a6990055ea1dc4a7052a0a66faa75b968c8e0c39a5374e033de33a9a" :answer/id #uuid "75004e4f-4347-566a-93bc-5ec3165d4191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection/e9f448bb65e82945dc599f862c2a07a6795f6b59531ba3cb1ae52398bec3bf7b" :answer/id #uuid "ba1f4e6a-c517-564f-8117-b15c49f6e64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection/df5e315860448f0143299572af17309a9892a83bd2489596fca0983f2aaf502f" :answer/id #uuid "979571ca-915c-5685-beef-08643dcf7de0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba972794-8086-5ed5-92ec-1729404e8d5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128499/selection/e9f448bb65e82945dc599f862c2a07a6795f6b59531ba3cb1ae52398bec3bf7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-128499/selection/f713e3c51be20750b1705399d88e20c65c6db6c19140d6bc7085e3e11b48f828" "q-128499/selection/2bf6099f6a9973b8307e08f883a440474edbb996ec474204a39fc02ae75563ab" "q-128499/selection/4d0ae1d7a6990055ea1dc4a7052a0a66faa75b968c8e0c39a5374e033de33a9a" "q-128499/selection/e9f448bb65e82945dc599f862c2a07a6795f6b59531ba3cb1ae52398bec3bf7b" "q-128499/selection/df5e315860448f0143299572af17309a9892a83bd2489596fca0983f2aaf502f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128499" :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128499/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128499"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection/9072e8f4597124bd09e3fede5e90577b1dc6b03186caba9c6efa217db8e6e250" :answer/id #uuid "628f16d5-4c7c-5663-81c5-ace18aa15b41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,2,-3⟩+s⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection/537e6f48b17f1cc1f93a0ca74ef13a06cad63babca197a4e539bba85ab71e56b" :answer/id #uuid "c7164b4a-10ca-55f8-90a8-29f0a6e48dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection/21c23afb400b5ecde4e1b3eb66e299e52cada41d68e41227ea75e59a02ad68a8" :answer/id #uuid "65db0400-cb51-5d1c-95bc-13b40540e6c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection/a04b055eb7142c579a471482183cb089409f5856fdbf00750e630d6755ecc35d" :answer/id #uuid "5b0c69f1-e39d-58cd-a058-b54a076c1d09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+t⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection/83b2267301fa210aa42eb9bd6eee66da01bab64d0e3804e8caa87cc70d364e32" :answer/id #uuid "5fd42a51-87db-5444-a542-250cdefdd488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-1,0,3⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "446c8cfe-5df2-5c5b-9dde-e9903f8903ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70976/selection/537e6f48b17f1cc1f93a0ca74ef13a06cad63babca197a4e539bba85ab71e56b" :answer-field/choices ["q-70976/selection/9072e8f4597124bd09e3fede5e90577b1dc6b03186caba9c6efa217db8e6e250" "q-70976/selection/537e6f48b17f1cc1f93a0ca74ef13a06cad63babca197a4e539bba85ab71e56b" "q-70976/selection/21c23afb400b5ecde4e1b3eb66e299e52cada41d68e41227ea75e59a02ad68a8" "q-70976/selection/a04b055eb7142c579a471482183cb089409f5856fdbf00750e630d6755ecc35d" "q-70976/selection/83b2267301fa210aa42eb9bd6eee66da01bab64d0e3804e8caa87cc70d364e32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70976" :question/id #uuid "8741dd2e-af66-5ff8-a395-814964cd05f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70976" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and $r=⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨-1,0,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-